WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Configuring the core RAG pipeline: defining LLM, embedding,
and reranker models for optimal retrieval and generation.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Managing user accounts and setting daily token caps to control
operational costs in an enterprise-scale AI deployment.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Engineering and versioning system prompts to enforce behavioral
constraints and ensure consistent output quality across domains.

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Orchestrating knowledge domains: mapping specific Elasticsearch indices
to local or cloud LLMs based on confidentiality and latency requirements.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Implementing granular Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to restrict
user access to specific knowledge categories and sensitive data.

6
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Initiating a streaming chat session; real-time GPU utilization confirms
on-premise inference using llama.cpp with Qwen3.6-35B-A3B.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Demonstrating conversational branching: editing a previous prompt to
explore alternative responses while maintaining context continuity.

8
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Verifying answer accuracy by inspecting the retrieved source document
that served as the ground truth for the generated response.

9
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Comparing parallel conversation branches side-by-side to evaluate
different reasoning paths and response variations.

10
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Enforcing domain boundaries: the system correctly refuses to answer
queries outside its authorized knowledge scope as per admin policy.

11
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Collecting user feedback via like/dislike mechanisms and displaying
real-time token consumption metrics for cost transparency.

12
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Validating security policies: general queries are blocked in restricted
domains but answered normally when switching to the public index.

13
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Leveraging multimodal capabilities: analyzing uploaded screenshots
and providing visual grounding for UI-related technical questions.

14
00:01:42.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Exporting conversation history to multiple formats including PDF,
Word, and print-ready layouts for offline documentation and reporting.

15
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Generating dynamic Mermaid flowcharts from natural language requests
to visualize complex installation processes and technical workflows.

16
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Displaying overridden source documents where the system intelligently
presents relevant forms instead of raw text for better user utility.

17
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Contrasting domain-specific responses: comparing generic software
installation steps against PetroPars' internal procedural guidelines.

18
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Providing direct citations to source materials, allowing users to
verify facts by viewing original document excerpts and page numbers.

19
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Executing secure on-premise inference with local CUDA acceleration
to ensure sensitive corporate data never leaves the infrastructure.

20
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.000
Switching to cloud API inference for non-sensitive tasks, achieving
significantly lower latency with zero local GPU resource consumption.